  {
   "id": 519463,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Price is $45,600, residual price is $21,312.50, 24-month lease, APR is 11.7%.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>You need to find the money factor first.</p>\n<p>The money factor (MF) is <span data-math=\"{\\rm{MF}} = \\frac{{{\\rm{APR}}}}{{2400}}\"></span>, where APR is the annual percentage rate as a decimal.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\rm{MF}} = \\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.117}}}}{{2400}} = {\\rm{ }}0.00004875\"></span></p>\n<p>The payment, <i>PMT</i>, for a lease is <span data-math=\"PMT = \\frac{{\\left( {P - R} \\right)}}{n} + \\left( {P + R} \\right) \\times \\left( {{\\rm{MF}}} \\right)\"></span>, where <i>P</i> is the price paid for the car, <i>R</i> is the residual value of the car after the <i>n</i> months of the lease, and MF is the money factor of the lease.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"PMT = \\frac{{\\left( {45,600 - 21,312.50} \\right)}}{{24}} + \\left( {45,600 + 21,312.50} \\right) \\times \\left( {{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.00004875}}} \\right) = \\$1,015.25\"></span></p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$1,015.25"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
